 /*
- * Copyright (C) 2017 starterkit.ru
+ * PicoCalc PWM audio (U8, mono, 8 kHz) for the Luckfox Lyra
  *
- * Based on simple driver for PWM (Pulse Width Modulator) controller
- * Sascha Hauer <s.hauer@pengutronix.de>
+ * Based on the driver by starterkit.ru / hiro, reworked:
+ *  - standby: while nothing plays (or muted) the output fades softly to 0 and
+ *    stays there - no idle noise, nothing at all at boot
+ *  - when a program starts playing, the output fades softly up to the middle
+ *    (50 %) first (S-curve, 0.25 s), so there is no pop
+ *  - after each sound the level glides back to the middle instead of jumping
+ *  - the timer is set up once and never started twice (fixes the hang that
+ *    caused knocking/noise)
+ *  - late timer calls skip samples instead of stretching the sound
+ *  - runtime mute via a module parameter (soft, no pop)
